# WN22-CC-000210: Windows Server 2022 Autoplay must be turned off for nonvolume devices.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: high
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-cc-000210-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `critical`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Autoplay must be turned off for nonvolume devices.`
    description `Allowing AutoPlay to execute may introduce malicious code to a system. AutoPlay begins reading from a drive as soon as media is inserted into the drive. As a result, the setup file of programs or music on audio media may start. This setting will disable AutoPlay for nonvolume devices, such as Media Transfer Protocol (MTP) devices.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,high,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:CM-7(2)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> AutoPlay Policies >> Disallow Autoplay for nonvolume devices to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by setting registry value 'NoAutoplayfornonVolume' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Explorer' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_CM_7_2 `Windows Server implements CM-7(2) by setting registry value 'NoAutoplayfornonVolume' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Explorer' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Explorer`
        name `NoAutoplayfornonVolume`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
